From f4670b1c4bf1cfaf9e40bb3c4390b72b89962968 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:26:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gweb: Look for the proxy scheme in the copy of the
 proxy URL

parse_url() copies the proxy URL into scheme and then means to split it
at "://", but searched the caller's proxy string instead of the copy.
For a proxy given with a scheme ("http://host:port") that wrote a NUL
into the caller's string, which is GWeb's own web->proxy, and compared
the unsplit copy against "http", so the request failed with -EINVAL and
every later request saw the proxy cut down to the bare scheme. A proxy
without a scheme was not affected.

Search the copy, as for the request URL above. ConnMan removed the same
mistake as part of its parse_url() rewrite in commit 35b9bec4248f
("gweb: Refactor 'parse_request_and_proxy_urls'."); that rewrite is not
taken here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gweb/gweb.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gweb/gweb.c b/gweb/gweb.c
index 4293b57..5030b86 100644
--- a/gweb/gweb.c
+++ b/gweb/gweb.c
@@ -1157,7 +1157,7 @@ static int parse_url(struct web_session *session,
 	if (scheme == NULL)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	host = strstr(proxy, "://");
+	host = strstr(scheme, "://");
 	if (host != NULL) {
 		*host = '\0';
 		host += 3;
-- 
